  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">"Cheezen jabtak perfect na ho, theek nhi lagti!"

At <a class="link" href="https://in.linkedin.com/company/apnahq?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>apna</a>, rooms aren’t named randomly.
They’re named after stories that reflect how we think and work.

Whenever someone enters this room, they know the expectation.
Come in with a goal. Leave with progress.

That is how we operate every day. A lot of hustle, a lot of ownership, and a strong belief that the right opportunity can change someone’s life. Especially in a country like India, where access can make all the difference, that responsibility means everything to us.

Because if it’s not meaningful, it’s not done.
This is how we build. This is who we are.

P.S. - Here’s a picture of Himanshu infront our Lakshya war room just before a meeting.

