  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        attributed-text-segment-list__content-truncated" dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Most candidates answer “strengths and weaknesses” like they are filling a form.

Quick learner. Detail-oriented. Perfectionist.
It sounds safe. It also sounds like everyone else.
Interviewers are not looking for labels. They are listening for self-awareness, proof, and improvement.

A strong answer does three things:
Names a real strength
Backs it with a specific moment
Owns a weakness and shows what you are doing to manage it.

That is the difference between sounding rehearsed and sounding credible.
Practice smarter with AI Job Prep.

Try it here: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gqnKGn4X?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gqnKGn4X</a>
